<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Sept M3 money supply grows 14.45 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Sept M3 money supply grows 14.45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 14.45 percent in September, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>August M3 growth was revised to 15.40 percent from a preliminary 15.51 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 17.94 percent, preliminary figures showed, against a revised 17.70 percent in August.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economist forecast M3 would grow at a rate of 15.1 percent in September, while they expected private sector credit extension to come in at 17.3.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>Sept 1996 preliminary M3 growth -- 14.45 percent</p>
<p>Sept 1996 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 17.94 percent</p>
<p>					   Aug '96		Jul '96</p>
<p>M3  revised			    15.40		  14.72</p>
<p>M2    &quot;				  19.62		  18.10</p>
<p>M1    &quot;				  31.55		  28.72</p>
<p>Private sector credit growth     17.70		  18.86</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (rand millions)</p>
<p>			    Sept '96(prel) Aug '96 (rev) Jul '96 (rev)</p>
<p>M3 unadjusted	   308.35	   306.44	  302.39</p>
<p>M3 seasonally adj.    308.97	   308.03	  305.95</p>
<p>Private sector credit 355.37	   349.40	  346.84</p>
<p>M3 annualised growth rate from base of guideline</p>
<p>			     15.84	    17.20	   18.27</p>
<p>(1996 guideline range 6-10 pct)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
